# The list is made by whoever reads `steps` first: the word is empty in the dead zone, holds a mark from the declaration on, and then the list. Each turn read the word, tested for the mark, and checked the dead zone.
# In front of the loop the word is read once: empty: the other copy . the mark: the list is made here, which nobody sees . and from there on the variable holds it: no turn of the typed copy reads the word.
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK-NEXT: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=absent
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=undefined
# CHECK: = PutModuleVariable
# CHECK: frequency=Rare isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = CheckInitialized {{*}}name="steps"
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = CheckInitialized
# CHECK-NOT: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK: Return
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 0 -1 0 4
